WEBVTT

00:01.429 --> 00:05.085
<i>♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪</i>

00:05.156 --> 00:08.311
<i>♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:08.369 --> 00:11.762
<i>♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.933 --> 00:14.785
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.934 --> 00:18.224
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.369 --> 00:21.503
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.604 --> 00:23.102
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.167 --> 00:24.745
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:31.088 --> 00:34.367
♪♪

00:36.774 --> 00:38.017
Hey, Meg. What are you up to?

00:38.092 --> 00:40.446
Not much. Just finished
an angel food cake.

00:40.563 --> 00:43.463
Might go out to the trash, see
if there's any possums to kiss.

00:43.533 --> 00:45.033
I was just out there.

00:46.797 --> 00:48.577
Oh, come on,
it's your senior year.

00:48.635 --> 00:50.554
Somebody must be having a party
or something.

00:50.612 --> 00:51.757
Well, there's one.

00:51.815 --> 00:53.781
But... I wasn't invited.

00:53.839 --> 00:55.272
Well, so what? Go crash it.

00:55.330 --> 00:56.830
Nah. Not my style.

00:56.888 --> 00:59.671
And what do you care?
Do you want the TV or something?

01:00.671 --> 01:04.179
What? No, no. I want...
I want to see you have fun.

01:04.284 --> 01:06.799
Come on, you should go,
you know? Let loose a little.

01:07.132 --> 01:08.960
You know what? You're right.

01:09.043 --> 01:10.803
<i>Maybe I will give it a shot.</i>

01:10.877 --> 01:12.405
Yeah. How awkward could it be?

01:12.600 --> 01:14.176
Can't be worse
than waving at someone

01:14.257 --> 01:15.998
who doesn't wave back at you.

01:19.200 --> 01:21.327
<i>- No, not you.
- Oh. Sorry.</i>

01:21.429 --> 01:23.288
<i>In fact, everyone but you.</i>

01:23.404 --> 01:24.850
Hi, everyone but him!

01:24.923 --> 01:26.115
Hi!

01:30.264 --> 01:33.792
Lou, I like you a lot, but
I-I think that's the last tape

01:33.850 --> 01:36.030
of you having sex with
your girlfriend I want to see.

01:36.162 --> 01:37.271
Suit yourself.

01:37.343 --> 01:39.538
All right, I got to get over
to my mom's wake.

01:39.618 --> 01:40.894
Oh, right, yeah. Crap.

01:40.952 --> 01:42.199
Ugh. Sorry again.

01:42.317 --> 01:44.218
- Oof. Cancer.
- Car accident.

01:44.284 --> 01:45.800
No, I know, I just, I'm...

01:45.858 --> 01:48.285
saying it feels like
everyone's getting cancer.

01:48.691 --> 01:50.166
You know, Bowie.

01:55.161 --> 01:58.299
<i>Time to get creepay...</i>

02:00.588 --> 02:02.350
Huh. Kid family.

02:13.200 --> 02:14.795
What a scumbag.

02:18.966 --> 02:20.174
Aw...

02:22.600 --> 02:24.023
Because I'm working all day!

02:24.080 --> 02:27.470
Oh, yeah? Well, here's what
I think of your stupid work!

02:27.579 --> 02:28.982
Don't you do that!

02:29.042 --> 02:30.610
Fiona, don't you...

02:32.426 --> 02:34.126
Is that Principal Shepherd?

02:34.530 --> 02:36.927
Wow, that looks like
a rocky relationship.

02:37.308 --> 02:39.106
"Rocky relationship."

02:41.364 --> 02:42.784
Ha-ha!

02:46.114 --> 02:48.083
Oh, come on, Brian.

02:48.153 --> 02:49.451
Don't comment or like it.

02:49.526 --> 02:51.849
It's a hard lesson,
but one he has to learn.

02:52.094 --> 02:54.778
♪♪ Electronic dance music playing...

02:54.835 --> 02:57.122
♪♪

03:01.915 --> 03:04.216
♪♪ Electronic dance music resumes...

03:04.535 --> 03:08.208
All right, ladies,
time to mingle.

03:08.298 --> 03:10.881
<i>Hey. You guys
talking Big Bang over here?</i>

03:11.047 --> 03:12.381
<i>Big Bang Theory?</i>

03:12.534 --> 03:14.804
No? Any Bangers over here?

03:15.137 --> 03:16.137
No?

03:16.474 --> 03:17.599
Well, I've tried everything.

03:17.657 --> 03:20.310
We just don't have anything
in common with these guys.

03:20.576 --> 03:24.950
Maybe... we don't need
anything in common with them.

03:27.803 --> 03:29.959
Meg, come on, don't go crazy.

03:30.110 --> 03:31.599
Damn, that's hot!

03:33.720 --> 03:35.319
That was just lucky.

03:35.377 --> 03:36.607
Oh, yeah?

03:41.044 --> 03:44.037
Wow! Meg's so good
at casually tossing bottles

03:44.099 --> 03:45.756
over her shoulder
so they land upright!

03:45.818 --> 03:47.268
And that's very popular
right now,

03:47.326 --> 03:49.395
because we've
run out of things on Earth.

03:49.561 --> 03:52.013
Meg, that was amazing!

03:52.110 --> 03:54.326
What can I say?
I'm full of surprises.

03:54.443 --> 03:56.607
<i>Like the end
of The Usual Suspects.</i>

03:56.879 --> 04:00.459
♪♪

04:03.854 --> 04:06.357
He was gay the whole time!

04:09.865 --> 04:11.462
<i>♪ Boughs of holly ♪</i>

04:11.529 --> 04:12.506
<i>♪ Rockin' around... ♪</i>

04:12.564 --> 04:14.097
Okay, they're obviously home.

04:14.208 --> 04:16.795
<i>You'd have to be dumb
to try to rob that place.</i>

04:19.668 --> 04:21.376
Oh, yes!

04:29.809 --> 04:31.869
I hate the guy, but he's good.

04:39.727 --> 04:40.860
Oh, my God.

04:41.224 --> 04:43.681
What the... what the hell
is going on over there?

04:43.827 --> 04:45.093
Did he...

04:46.650 --> 04:48.423
<i>- Hello. -
- Hey, Stewie, it's me.</i>

04:48.481 --> 04:49.509
You got a second?

04:49.567 --> 04:50.892
<i>Brian? Hang on.</i>

04:51.009 --> 04:52.631
<i>Hey, keep it down,
you screwballs.</i>

04:52.693 --> 04:54.635
<i>Here, let me just go
somewhere a little quieter.</i>

04:54.693 --> 04:57.247
<i>Oh, yeah, right. I'm the screwball.</i>

04:57.392 --> 04:59.397
You and friends
say "screwball" a lot.

04:59.455 --> 05:01.855
That's what happens when
you run with a screwy crowd.

05:01.913 --> 05:02.834
What's up with you?

05:02.907 --> 05:04.162
Stewie, I think...

05:04.381 --> 05:06.662
I think Principal Shepherd
killed his wife.

05:06.717 --> 05:08.216
What? What are you
talking about?

05:08.279 --> 05:10.310
I think I saw him
getting rid of her body.

05:10.443 --> 05:12.412
And carrying a bag
with something heavy in it.

05:12.479 --> 05:14.951
And... and there was red liquid
dripping from it.

05:15.018 --> 05:16.460
Okay, I've got to see this
for myself.

05:16.517 --> 05:18.193
Don't do anything.
I'm coming over.

05:18.310 --> 05:19.596
Hey, listen,
you-you don't think...

05:19.653 --> 05:21.622
you don't think you
could snag a couple of rolls

05:21.689 --> 05:23.084
of toilet paper, could you?

05:25.123 --> 05:27.230
<i>- Stewie?
- I'm here. I just wanted you</i>

05:27.297 --> 05:29.451
<i>to have to sit with those words
for a minute.</i>

05:33.224 --> 05:34.748
Kids, dinner's ready!

05:34.806 --> 05:35.863
"Dinner's ready."

05:35.920 --> 05:37.124
Shut up.

05:37.182 --> 05:40.218
Little of the old schnappster
ought to get me right.

05:41.477 --> 05:43.638
'Ey... Chrissay!

05:43.755 --> 05:46.292
Well, that's
delightfully informal, Meg.

05:46.350 --> 05:47.888
How the heck are ya?

05:47.999 --> 05:50.663
♪♪

05:51.326 --> 05:52.956
So, what are you kids
doing in school?

05:53.023 --> 05:55.627
I got in trouble for saying
something "insensitive"

05:55.685 --> 05:56.881
to trans kids.

05:56.939 --> 05:59.018
- What'd you say?
- Well, a few them started

05:59.076 --> 06:01.205
this a cappella group,
and they're all kind of chubby.

06:01.263 --> 06:05.367
So I said, "You guys should
call yourselves the Trans Fats."

06:06.379 --> 06:08.256
Meg, you'll sit
next to me this evening.

06:08.373 --> 06:11.304
- But, Dad...
- I'm sorry, Chris. You've fallen out of favor.

06:11.396 --> 06:12.670
Perhaps forever.

06:18.060 --> 06:19.615
Oh, Stewie,
thank God you're here.

06:19.782 --> 06:21.748
There's a seagull
in your hallway.

06:21.869 --> 06:23.001
Listen, what are we gonna do

06:23.059 --> 06:24.623
about this
Principal Shepherd thing?

06:25.115 --> 06:28.076
Look, all you know is that
the guy was carrying a wet bag.

06:28.162 --> 06:29.701
It doesn't mean
he killed his wife.

06:29.763 --> 06:31.558
You're building this whole theory...

06:31.615 --> 06:32.759
What is that noise?

06:33.006 --> 06:34.196
It's a news alert.

06:34.513 --> 06:37.776
"Fiona Shepherd, wife of James
Woods High School principal

06:37.834 --> 06:40.615
John Shepherd,
has been reported missing."

06:40.732 --> 06:42.846
<i>Oh, my God, maybe he did do it.</i>

06:42.904 --> 06:45.091
You know, there are
some bad people in this world.

06:45.162 --> 06:46.537
<i>Hey, you don't got
to tell me that.</i>

06:46.595 --> 06:48.216
I learned that in Fight Club.

06:48.372 --> 06:51.107
All right, Stewie, what's
the first rule of Fight Club?

06:51.193 --> 06:52.732
G-string underwear.

06:52.790 --> 06:55.154
No. It's "don't talk
about Fight Club."

06:55.267 --> 06:57.740
Oh. Well, I really blew it.

07:00.214 --> 07:02.859
♪♪

07:04.256 --> 07:06.716
Hey-o! What's up in this piece?

07:06.806 --> 07:08.076
You're getting home late.

07:08.134 --> 07:10.892
Yeah. We were hanging out
in the woods, and...

07:12.657 --> 07:15.559
this one girl pushed
another girl over

07:15.626 --> 07:16.943
while she was peeing.

07:17.001 --> 07:18.740
They fought,
and then the cops came.

07:18.798 --> 07:20.138
Meg, this is important.

07:20.522 --> 07:22.162
Did she fall in the pee?

07:22.293 --> 07:23.695
I can smell your breath.

07:23.753 --> 07:25.385
You've been drinking,
haven't you?

07:25.443 --> 07:29.045
No! Geez, Mom, get off my back.

07:29.388 --> 07:31.513
Peter, I think
she's doing booze.

07:31.571 --> 07:32.699
What should we do?

07:32.759 --> 07:34.459
Lois, she's just being
a teenager.

07:34.517 --> 07:37.427
We don't know she's, like, for
sure, definitely been drinking.

07:37.529 --> 07:39.138
I found this in her room.

07:39.207 --> 07:40.873
My little girl's a drunk!

07:40.978 --> 07:44.682
Oh, my God,
where did we go wrong?

07:47.066 --> 07:49.754
♪♪

07:51.387 --> 07:52.825
Meg, we need to talk.

07:52.883 --> 07:55.173
What, Mom? But I know
what you're gonna say,

07:55.231 --> 07:56.805
and I know how
you're gonna say it.

07:56.863 --> 07:58.163
- Oh, really?
- Yep.

07:58.256 --> 07:59.663
I don't want you drinkin'

07:59.720 --> 08:02.024
or your life's
gonna go down the crappah.

08:02.662 --> 08:03.794
That's not bad.

08:03.833 --> 08:05.795
I-I mean,
I sound nothing like that,

08:05.913 --> 08:07.647
but it's a fun character. Heh.

08:07.710 --> 08:08.888
But this is serious.

08:08.955 --> 08:10.819
Alcoholism runs in our family.

08:10.926 --> 08:13.762
<i>Hey, I'm just glad
something runs in this family.</i>

08:15.170 --> 08:16.505
I don't mean to...

08:16.913 --> 08:19.532
I-I don't mean to laugh, okay?
But that was funny.

08:19.599 --> 08:21.102
Mom, I'm just having fun.

08:21.169 --> 08:24.170
I'm finally known as something
other than "the chubby girl

08:24.241 --> 08:25.941
who put the lunch lady
in a headlock."

08:25.999 --> 08:27.964
And besides, Dad's the one

08:28.022 --> 08:29.518
who pushed me
into going to that party.

08:29.575 --> 08:31.452
Oh, he did, did he?

08:32.948 --> 08:34.585
Son of a bitch.
What was that?

08:34.717 --> 08:37.150
I don't know. Someone
must've messed something up.

08:37.303 --> 08:39.605
Listen, you need to talk to Meg
about her drinking.

08:39.663 --> 08:40.745
What? Why me?

08:40.803 --> 08:42.261
Because you're the one
who told her

08:42.319 --> 08:43.888
to start going
to these parties.

08:43.955 --> 08:45.550
Okay, fine.

08:45.608 --> 08:47.560
I guess it's just something
I got to deal with.

08:47.627 --> 08:50.202
Like the flush
of a high-powered toilet.

08:53.759 --> 08:56.933
♪♪

08:58.707 --> 09:01.520
So, you plan on going back
at that banana, huh?

09:01.633 --> 09:03.364
So the bastard killed his wife,

09:03.481 --> 09:04.989
and then reported her missing.

09:05.114 --> 09:07.379
I-I got to...
I got to call the cops.

09:09.332 --> 09:11.481
- Quahog Police.
- Joe, Joe, it's Brian.

09:11.637 --> 09:12.860
Listen, I have
to tell you something.

09:12.917 --> 09:14.528
I-I'm pretty sure

09:14.590 --> 09:16.215
Principal Shepherd
killed his wife.

09:16.309 --> 09:18.938
That's a serious accusation.
Do you have any proof?

09:18.996 --> 09:20.793
I have something better
than proof:

09:20.965 --> 09:24.087
rank suspicion born out
of boredom and loneliness.

09:24.145 --> 09:26.230
Sorry, that's just not enough
for us to go on.

09:26.457 --> 09:29.707
You must be pretty tired
from thinking about all this.

09:29.864 --> 09:32.196
- You ever get bags under your eyes?
- What?

09:32.254 --> 09:35.137
I've been using this eye cream,
it's done wonders for me.

09:35.200 --> 09:37.493
It's made by a company
called Rodan and Fields.

09:37.551 --> 09:38.848
Have you heard of them, Brian?

09:38.981 --> 09:40.110
Yeah, I-I think, uh...

09:40.168 --> 09:41.462
Oh, they make terrific stuff.

09:41.520 --> 09:42.985
In fact, I was such a fan,

09:43.043 --> 09:45.215
I became a sales consultant
for the company.

09:45.278 --> 09:46.688
Listen, Joe, I got to run.

09:46.746 --> 09:48.712
I'm hosting a little
get-together tomorrow night,

09:48.770 --> 09:51.001
If you want to stop by.
There's gonna be pizza

09:51.059 --> 09:54.496
and soft drinks, then a man's
gonna talk about the whole line.

09:54.575 --> 09:56.731
Can I go ahead
and confirm your attendance?

09:56.798 --> 09:58.348
Well, that was no help.

09:58.434 --> 10:00.575
What if I go over there
and try to find some evidence

10:00.668 --> 10:02.199
- that he did it?
- All right, fine.

10:02.257 --> 10:03.368
But you have to be careful.

10:03.426 --> 10:05.071
Don't worry,
he won't have any idea.

10:05.129 --> 10:06.290
I'll be more discreet

10:06.348 --> 10:08.973
than a guy standing by himself
in the ocean.

10:10.812 --> 10:12.027
Hey, are you peeing?

10:12.085 --> 10:13.121
No.

10:13.343 --> 10:14.509
Are you pooping?

10:14.567 --> 10:16.212
I'm just trying
to enjoy the day.

10:16.270 --> 10:17.816
Why don't you
go bother that guy?

10:17.883 --> 10:20.371
Summer's blown by, huh?

10:20.663 --> 10:23.208
♪♪

10:23.825 --> 10:25.809
So, your mom says
you've been drinking.

10:25.909 --> 10:27.426
Yeah, like, a little bit, but...

10:27.512 --> 10:29.176
but it's nothing
you have to worry about.

10:29.254 --> 10:31.317
Look, I-I was young,
too, you know.

10:31.402 --> 10:34.532
I-I remember going to parties,
walking up with a six pack.

10:34.590 --> 10:37.457
You're so excited to get there,
you start jogging a little.

10:37.567 --> 10:40.207
Your friends are all there,
and they're so happy to see you,

10:40.285 --> 10:41.934
they're practically cheering
your name.

10:42.027 --> 10:44.587
And then "Mony Mony" comes on
at just the right time.

10:44.645 --> 10:45.837
And everyone's dancing,

10:45.895 --> 10:48.871
and-and Laura Hallston's jugs
are just slamming into you.

10:48.942 --> 10:50.418
You don't have a care
in the world,

10:50.485 --> 10:53.785
and if all of it came to an end
right then and there, so be it.

10:54.105 --> 10:55.371
Well, you're my daughter,

10:55.473 --> 10:57.551
and I don't want
any of that for you.

10:58.121 --> 11:01.215
Hey, you want to see where I was
sitting when you were born?

11:05.004 --> 11:07.395
Yeah, I still think
about Laura a lot.

11:07.660 --> 11:09.582
You were already drinking
tonight, weren't you?

11:10.043 --> 11:11.134
A little.

11:11.192 --> 11:13.471
Well, I can't talk
to a drunk person if I'm sober.

11:13.538 --> 11:15.527
Hey, Jerome,
can I get a beer, please?

11:15.874 --> 11:18.168
<i>But now I'm starting
to sober up,</i>

11:18.254 --> 11:20.979
so I'm gonna need one
to keep an even playing field.

11:21.046 --> 11:23.192
All right,
but it stays between us.

11:23.254 --> 11:24.550
And what if they card you?

11:24.636 --> 11:26.792
Don't worry. I got it covered.

11:29.223 --> 11:31.082
Wow. That's really good.

11:31.145 --> 11:34.062
Right?! Jerome, make it two!

11:36.798 --> 11:40.009
<i>♪ My girl wants
to party all the time ♪</i>

11:40.067 --> 11:43.947
<i>♪ Party all the time,
party all the time ♪</i>

11:44.048 --> 11:47.029
<i>♪ My girl wants
to party all the time ♪</i>

11:47.087 --> 11:50.439
<i>♪ Party all the time ♪</i>

11:58.553 --> 12:03.451
<i>♪ I buy you champagne and roses,
put diamonds on your finger ♪</i>

12:03.509 --> 12:04.501
<i>♪ Diamonds on your finger ♪</i>

12:04.559 --> 12:06.100
<i>♪ Party all the time ♪</i>

12:06.160 --> 12:10.650
<i>♪ Ooh, ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh,
ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh ♪</i>

12:10.712 --> 12:13.743
<i>♪ My girl wants
to party all the time ♪</i>

12:13.837 --> 12:17.634
<i>♪ Party all the time ♪</i>

12:17.719 --> 12:20.759
<i>♪ Yeah. ♪</i>

12:25.931 --> 12:27.550
All right, he's gone.

12:27.728 --> 12:30.163
Now, if I give the word, you've
got to get out of there, okay?

12:30.220 --> 12:31.447
Got it.

12:31.819 --> 12:33.386
Oh, my God!

12:33.453 --> 12:34.548
What? What is it?

12:34.649 --> 12:36.365
He sleeps in a bunk bed!

12:36.424 --> 12:38.314
Are you kidding me?!
Who is this guy?!

12:38.454 --> 12:40.611
Wait a second. Is that...?

12:40.720 --> 12:42.232
Bri, I'm gonna put you down
for a sec.

12:42.290 --> 12:44.333
Stewie, no! Don't.

12:49.526 --> 12:51.301
Stewie, get out of there!

12:51.469 --> 12:53.501
Stewie! Stewie!

12:53.676 --> 12:56.544
Got to get his attention.

12:57.785 --> 12:59.887
Man, just short.

13:02.492 --> 13:04.275
Oh, God.

13:17.623 --> 13:18.628
Domino's.

13:18.686 --> 13:21.290
Oh, good.

13:21.749 --> 13:23.335
Medium pie, ten wings.

13:23.421 --> 13:25.152
Is the blue cheese
dressing in there?

13:25.210 --> 13:26.559
Thanks a lot. Have a good one.

13:33.575 --> 13:35.199
Mmm.

13:42.089 --> 13:45.032
He got out! Ha, ha!
Yes, Stewie!

13:56.905 --> 13:58.016
Oh, crap.

13:58.376 --> 14:00.014
Oh, my, that was close.

14:00.134 --> 14:02.975
Stewie, he saw you! He saw you
leaving his apartment!

14:03.042 --> 14:05.240
Oh. Well... so what?

14:05.298 --> 14:07.040
He doesn't know
what we're doing.

14:10.753 --> 14:12.770
Ah!
What? What is it?

14:14.727 --> 14:16.053
Well, that's...

14:16.220 --> 14:17.587
that's not good.

14:28.903 --> 14:30.482
Dad? Dad, wake up!

14:30.540 --> 14:32.248
- Huh? What happened?
- I don't know!

14:32.306 --> 14:33.958
We must have stolen this boat
last night.

14:34.016 --> 14:36.509
I-I have no idea
where the hell we are!

14:37.970 --> 14:39.814
Oh, no, my cell phone's dead!

14:40.119 --> 14:41.704
I got a little bit
of juice left,

14:41.762 --> 14:43.990
so we can either
A, call someone,

14:44.048 --> 14:45.696
maybe they answer,
maybe they can help,

14:45.782 --> 14:49.120
or B, we can definitely
switch faces.

14:49.446 --> 14:51.692
Look at you!
Look at me!

14:51.852 --> 14:53.951
That's what this is!

14:54.009 --> 14:55.631
Oh, we're gonna die.

15:02.123 --> 15:03.889
Dad, what are we gonna do?

15:03.964 --> 15:06.359
You think it's too early to tie
our shirts around our heads

15:06.417 --> 15:07.660
to show we're going insane?

15:07.772 --> 15:10.041
I mean it, Dad. This is serious.

15:10.116 --> 15:11.481
I did pants instead.

15:11.618 --> 15:13.944
Ugh! I don't feel so hot.

15:14.118 --> 15:15.615
What is wrong with me?

15:15.687 --> 15:17.748
Have you taken a break
since you started drinking?

15:17.826 --> 15:19.347
Not until right now.

15:19.451 --> 15:21.429
Do you feel like lying
on the couch, rubbing your eyes,

15:21.486 --> 15:23.531
while listening
to Lou Reed's "Perfect Day"?

15:23.598 --> 15:25.767
- Yes!
- Then I'll tell you what's wrong with you.

15:25.834 --> 15:26.880
You got a hangover.

15:26.990 --> 15:28.603
What can you do for a hangover?

15:28.670 --> 15:30.430
Well, Meg,
so I don't have to think

15:30.497 --> 15:31.795
about my throbbing headache,

15:31.862 --> 15:34.295
I try to think of
something else, like a riddle.

15:34.513 --> 15:37.101
Like, how would you describe
Chris O'Donnell?

15:37.168 --> 15:40.591
Huh. He's not tall or short.

15:40.834 --> 15:42.810
And he's not fat or thin.

15:43.091 --> 15:45.309
Well, he's not handsome or ugly.

15:45.677 --> 15:48.638
And he's not young or old.

15:48.700 --> 15:51.130
He's not loud or quiet.

15:51.318 --> 15:54.401
Uh, he's not memorable,
but-but I know who he is.

15:54.459 --> 15:56.416
Ah!
Thanks, Dad!

15:56.474 --> 15:57.999
I feel so much better.

15:58.057 --> 15:59.412
But you know who doesn't?

15:59.596 --> 16:00.865
Chris O'Donnell.

16:00.943 --> 16:02.446
Bye, dildo.

16:09.507 --> 16:11.997
Oh, no. Hard shoes on linoleum.

16:12.123 --> 16:13.268
That's a principal!

16:13.326 --> 16:15.232
Brian, a lot of people
live in this building,

16:15.326 --> 16:17.708
and you can't tell it's
a principal just from a walk.

16:19.580 --> 16:22.849
Excuse me? May I have
your attention, please?

16:22.916 --> 16:24.998
Okay, that's probably
a principal.

16:28.029 --> 16:30.318
Hey. How are you today?

16:30.584 --> 16:31.829
What can I do for you?

16:31.943 --> 16:33.092
What do you want from me?

16:33.159 --> 16:35.059
Listen, it's...
it's-it's not what you think.

16:35.126 --> 16:36.372
Then what is it?

16:36.431 --> 16:40.071
Well... I'm, um...
I'm actually doing a documentary

16:40.165 --> 16:41.755
about some
of the finest principals

16:41.813 --> 16:42.884
in the country, and...

16:42.980 --> 16:44.685
Ow! Continue.

16:44.743 --> 16:47.695
"Finest principals
in the country" and...

16:48.057 --> 16:49.509
Brian!

16:49.576 --> 16:51.451
Stewie! Help me!

16:52.028 --> 16:53.613
<i>How did I get here?</i>

16:53.751 --> 16:56.877
<i>Well, to answer that, you'd
have to go back a little while.</i>

16:56.935 --> 16:57.915
<i>We're not doing that!</i>

17:02.976 --> 17:04.324
We found this in a Dumpster

17:04.391 --> 17:06.121
behind Principal Shepherd's
building.

17:06.179 --> 17:07.826
That's it.
That's-that's the bag!

17:07.893 --> 17:09.749
I guarantee his wife's in there.

17:13.139 --> 17:14.511
- Ha!
- What's the matter, Rook?

17:14.581 --> 17:15.649
Too heavy for you?

17:15.707 --> 17:17.376
I've actually been a cop
for years.

17:17.434 --> 17:18.761
I have tummy cancer.

17:18.860 --> 17:21.159
Oh. Weird way to say that.

17:22.909 --> 17:25.034
What the hell? Bu-But I saw...

17:25.119 --> 17:26.351
Yeah, well, what is all this?

17:26.409 --> 17:27.480
Principal Shepherd,

17:27.547 --> 17:29.915
I think you've got
some explaining to do.

17:29.982 --> 17:32.558
Look, I tried to tell you,
I didn't kill my wife.

17:32.636 --> 17:35.159
She just texted me today
that she's moved out

17:35.245 --> 17:36.808
and she's banging my cousin,

17:36.894 --> 17:38.758
Pat Sajak's accountant,
by the way.

17:38.825 --> 17:40.355
It's a weird time to name drop.

17:40.413 --> 17:42.656
And the food, well,
I've been stealing it

17:42.714 --> 17:44.355
from the high school
to make ends meet.

17:44.441 --> 17:46.700
My life's "kinda brute,"
as the kids say.

17:46.767 --> 17:48.465
Sounds like
you've had a rough day.

17:48.532 --> 17:51.801
No wonder you've got those bags
under your eyes.

17:51.868 --> 17:56.206
Have you ever heard of a company
called Rodan and Fields?

17:58.558 --> 18:01.831
Ugh. Are all hangovers this bad?

18:01.995 --> 18:04.784
Yup, that's the deal
you make with the gods of fun.

18:04.862 --> 18:07.105
Every 72 hours, you lose a day.

18:07.292 --> 18:09.422
Dad, you're so sunburnt.

18:09.628 --> 18:11.737
I can't move
because it hurts too bad.

18:11.852 --> 18:13.675
Ugh. This is awful.

18:13.733 --> 18:16.027
We don't even know
if anyone's looking for us.

18:16.085 --> 18:18.042
Look, don't worry.
We're gonna be okay.

18:18.136 --> 18:19.932
This is why you shouldn't drink.

18:19.999 --> 18:22.354
Booze is nothing but trouble,
and you don't need it.

18:22.542 --> 18:24.089
You got a good brain
in your head.

18:24.304 --> 18:27.800
Thanks, Dad, and if this is what
drinking makes you feel like,

18:27.940 --> 18:29.417
you don't have
to worry about it.

18:29.487 --> 18:31.443
I am done with booze.

18:31.612 --> 18:33.347
Aw, I'm glad to hear that.

18:33.447 --> 18:35.312
And I'm sorry
I pushed it on you.

18:35.379 --> 18:37.886
I just...
I just wanted to watch TV.

18:38.268 --> 18:40.148
I don't want
to see you waste opportunities

18:40.206 --> 18:41.612
'cause you were out partying.

18:41.853 --> 18:43.256
That's what I did.

18:43.456 --> 18:45.289
You just worry about being you.

18:45.456 --> 18:46.690
Don't worry, Dad.

18:46.826 --> 18:48.839
I'll never be anything like you.

18:48.992 --> 18:50.864
That's my girl.

18:52.459 --> 18:54.201
Dad, look!

18:56.202 --> 18:58.806
Oh, my God.
Meg, we're saved!

19:04.628 --> 19:06.112
Thank God you found us.

19:06.206 --> 19:08.147
We're so glad
you picked us up...

19:08.300 --> 19:10.181
- Chris O'Donnell?
- That's right.

19:10.239 --> 19:12.910
And I hope
you like turbulence, dildos.

19:12.986 --> 19:14.851
<i>The actual Chris O'Donnell</i>

19:14.918 --> 19:17.356
<i>is not a Coast Guard
helicopter pilot.</i>

19:17.479 --> 19:19.870
<i>We assume
he's probably too short.</i>

19:24.643 --> 19:26.448
Oh, my God.
Brian, are you okay?

19:26.534 --> 19:27.634
Yeah, I'm fine.

19:27.807 --> 19:29.167
Annie, are you okay?

19:29.253 --> 19:31.784
So, Annie, are you okay?
Are you okay, Annie?

19:31.932 --> 19:33.304
What happened to her?

19:33.362 --> 19:34.542
She was hit by, uh...

19:34.612 --> 19:36.659
She was struck
by a smooth criminal.

19:36.801 --> 19:38.289
That was fun, Mom.

19:38.347 --> 19:40.909
We don't get to do a lot
of that kind of stuff together.

19:41.065 --> 19:43.581
Listen, Brian,
we want you to come home again.

19:43.716 --> 19:47.159
Oh, so the Twitter pariah
is finally welcome home?

19:47.276 --> 19:50.190
No, but the school board
hero dog is.

19:50.268 --> 19:51.690
It was all over the papers.

19:51.748 --> 19:55.679
You saved the school $206
from all the food they recovered

19:55.737 --> 19:57.354
from Principal Shepherd's
fridge.

19:57.417 --> 20:00.018
So... you really want me
to come home?

20:00.097 --> 20:02.495
They're still gonna serve
that food?

20:02.589 --> 20:04.268
Of course we do.

20:05.667 --> 20:07.128
Hey, where's everyone else?

20:07.214 --> 20:09.472
Oh, my God.
Peter, what happened?

20:09.682 --> 20:11.737
<i>What happened? A fair question.</i>

20:11.862 --> 20:14.214
<i>And to answer it,
we have to go back a ways.</i>

20:14.331 --> 20:16.449
<i>- Stop doing that thing!
- Aw.</i>

20:18.675 --> 20:21.286
♪♪

20:21.679 --> 20:24.547
Brian, I got to say, it's great
to have you home again, buddy.

20:24.605 --> 20:26.039
Well, it's great to be here.

20:26.170 --> 20:27.647
Living on my own was fun,

20:27.705 --> 20:29.612
but I couldn't stop thinking
about all the stuff

20:29.679 --> 20:31.308
I was missing
being away from you guys.

20:31.366 --> 20:33.146
Did you ever finish
that banana, Brian?

20:33.213 --> 20:36.100
And, Meg, I hope you learned
your lesson about drinking.

20:36.183 --> 20:39.530
Yeah, I think I'd rather
live my life as a loser

20:39.686 --> 20:41.459
than feel bad once in a while.

20:41.600 --> 20:44.358
<i>Well, I hope you know
that you're our loser.</i>

20:44.471 --> 20:45.928
Thanks, Mom.

20:53.772 --> 20:55.928
<i>If my life were better here,</i>

20:56.057 --> 20:59.967
<i>would I stop searching for it...
up there?</i>

20:59.968 --> 22:00.968
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru